1
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:30,960
Leaping lightly beyond the times

2
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:37,480
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

3
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:39,480
I wanna, time is a paradise

4
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:45,120
Wearing only the latest trends

5
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:49,220
Because your natural
face suits you even better

6
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,980
Let it rain

7
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:55,020
Everybody can do, we started running

8
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:58,240
Dreams never stop, you know

9
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:02,460
Let's set sail again tomorrow

10
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,340
Love you, one

11
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:06,140
Everybody can do

12
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:10,820
Even if we stick out a little,
it doesn't hurt

13
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,020
Holding onto a restless curiosity

14
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:17,900
Strong and high, stay up

15
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:30,720
Even the Chief is moved to tears.

16
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:40,080
Could you come out for a moment?

17
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:46,340
Yes, this is Ohara speaking.

18
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:48,440
Hello, this is Kakuda.

19
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:50,160
Are you her father?

20
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:51,120
May I speak to Hiromi?

21
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,060
It's you again.

22
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:54,800
I have no recollection of being called
"father" by you.

23
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:55,560
Father...

24
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:58,140
This is utterly displeasing.

25
00:01:58,140 --> 00:02:00,600
Dad, that call just now was from Hideo,
wasn't it?

26
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:04,160
He suddenly called me
"father," so I hung up on him.

27
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:07,660
How awful!
Even if you're my father, that's too much!

28
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:11,580
Hideo-san is calling all the way from America,
where he's on a business trip.

29
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:13,380
I don't know anything about that.

30
00:02:13,820 --> 00:02:15,100
Father...

31
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:23,600
When Hideo comes back from America,
I have something important to tell him.

32
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,903
Damn,

33
00:02:24,953 --> 00:02:27,660
I've caught a cold, I'm going to bed.

34
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:28,540
Dad.

35
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:31,443
Damn,

36
00:02:31,493 --> 00:02:35,160
I feel feverish, it's a cold, it's a cold.

37
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:37,480
Nice, a wedding dress

38
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,560
Hey, Reigo.

39
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:41,640
What?

40
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,360
W-what is it, Ryo-chan?

41
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:47,680
My butt's ripped open, sew it for me.

42
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,660
Ugh! You're ruining the mood!

43
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,820
Wow, Reiko-san, you're good at sewing too

44
00:02:57,820 --> 00:03:00,360
The guy who gets you as
his wife will be a lucky man.

45
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:04,600
Y-yeah, yeah, yeah. So that's why
you were looking at this kind of book?

46
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:08,520
Well, every girl loves wedding dresses,
you know.

47
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:11,900
Forget that, Ryo-chan. Shouldn't
you hurry up and get yourself a wife?

48
00:03:12,260 --> 00:03:15,020
No way, no thanks.
Marriage is only good at the very start.

49
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,140
I'm enjoying my single life.

50
00:03:18,940 --> 00:03:22,960
But watching you, senpai,
I feel more misery than enjoyment.

51
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:26,280
The real question isn't whether
a wife would come to you, is it?

52
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:28,540
That's cruel, you know,
saying the truth like that.

53
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,700
Shut up, and leave people's business alone.

54
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:36,320
Oh no, back to work, back to work!

55
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,560
That's that, then.

56
00:03:44,580 --> 00:03:45,920
Good work, everyone.

57
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:48,700
I'll stop by the station on my way home.

58
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,080
Leave the handover to you, Nakagawa.

59
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,940
Good work, sir.

60
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,440
Think I'll go home and take it easy.

61
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,280
Good evening.

62
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,080
Hiromi.

63
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:00,520
Long time no see.

64
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:02,040
Well, well.

65
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,420
Did you come all this
way to pick up the Chief?

66
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:07,620
Hello.

67
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:10,520
Chief?

68
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,020
Chief, where did he go?

69
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:14,400
Chief!

70
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,460
What, Chief, you're still here?

71
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:23,871
Dad, I have something
important to talk about,

72
00:04:23,921 --> 00:04:25,400
how about we get something to eat together?

73
00:04:25,640 --> 00:04:28,000
N-no way. I still have work to do.

74
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:29,980
Dad, please.

75
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:34,000
It can't be helped.
T-this work is important too.

76
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:37,600
Chief, didn't you just
say you were going home?

77
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,980
I changed my mind.

78
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:43,800
Come on, that's strange. Your daughter came
all the way to pick you up with her boyfriend.

79
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:45,960
I get it, you're just embarrassed.

80
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,460
Hiromi's at that age, after all,

81
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:51,260
so rather than eating with
a washed-up old dad like this,

82
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:53,260
she obviously wants to
eat with her boyfriend.

83
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:55,800
Chief, you should just be happy about it.

84
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:58,380
Dads should appreciate it while
they're still being invited.

85
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,740
Anyway, dads are just...

86
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:02,220
Shut up, it's none of your business.

87
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:03,700
I'm going on patrol.

88
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:06,560
Dad...

89
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:11,960
Hideo...

90
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:15,460
Hiromi-chan...

91
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:16,800
I'm sorry.

92
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:19,420
Dad won't even listen to me at all.

93
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:21,620
And there's no time left.

94
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:29,640
We've been dating since our student days.

95
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:30,740
Yes.

96
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:33,360
So he's finally proposing How wonderful.

97
00:05:33,940 --> 00:05:34,920
Well, how wonderful indeed.

98
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,500
Another sake, old man.

99
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:39,620
So what do you mean, there's no time?

100
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:43,180
It's just that Hideo has
been suddenly transferred.

101
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:46,660
I was hoping to talk to
him before then, but...

102
00:05:46,660 --> 00:05:50,060
Dad's being so stubborn,
he won't listen to me at all.

103
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:51,560
Hey, Dad, another round!

104
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:52,820
Yo-chan.

105
00:05:52,820 --> 00:05:54,640
Because the Chief is such a stubborn one.

106
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,500
Fine, we'll push him from our side too.

107
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,440
Thank you very much.

108
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:00,420
Please, I'm counting on you.

109
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,300
Speaking of Dad, it was my fault.

110
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:06,940
I got impatient and couldn't
think about how your father feels.

111
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:11,060
What do you mean, rushed?
He's being transferred that far away?

112
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:12,800
No, it's Hokkaido.

113
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:16,060
Sounds nice. The food's great,
and the sake and beer are good too.

114
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:19,400
How can you be so carefree?
It's not a vacation, you know.

115
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,700
So it's within Tokyo, then.

116
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:25,900
Did he make some blunder that
got him made to write a reprimand?

117
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:26,800
No.

118
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:30,040
Hideo's company is
headquartered in Hokkaido.

119
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:34,540
I should have mentioned it.
I work for a company like this.

120
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,960
Well then, it's fine, isn't it?

121
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:39,160
Here you go.

122
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:42,100
Software development for computer games?

123
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:45,820
Ever since he joined, he's been going
back and forth between America and Japan.

124
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:49,300
I thought he could finally settle down,
but now it's Hokkaido.

125
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:51,440
I can't do anything for Hiromi.

126
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,340
It's all right, don't worry about it.

127
00:06:53,960 --> 00:06:55,240
I'll be fine.

128
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:58,660
Even if we can't be together,
I'm very happy.

129
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,740
Hey, hey, hey!

130
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,140
Y-yes!

131
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:04,804
Your company,

132
00:07:04,854 --> 00:07:09,460
isn't it developing a game
called Campus Fairy Quest?

133
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,300
H-how do you know about that?

134
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,320
Ryo-chan loves games, so

135
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:16,200
even in the industry,
only a few people know about it.

136
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:16,906
What do you say?

137
00:07:16,956 --> 00:07:21,040
I'll introduce you to the Chief in
exchange for sending me a prototype, deal?

138
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:25,460
C-Campus Fairy is a bit...
if you like games...

139
00:07:26,020 --> 00:07:28,620
How about the buggy version of Nuppupu-ya 2?

140
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:36,720
Then how about Chest Hair Police? The
one you got before pre-orders even opened?

141
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:42,980
Then you've got Angel Hazard,
and you've even cleared it, right?

142
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:53,840
Then Poyo 4 Super, you cleared that and lent out the other one, why?
Then how about Aquanaut's Holiday, the one with the Tekken memory?

143
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,360
That's good.

144
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:57,300
Alright, leave it to me.

145
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:59,520
I'll introduce you to the Chief, no problem.

146
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,520
Really?

147
00:08:01,720 --> 00:08:04,220
So, about the game software,
you'll take care of that, got it?

148
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:04,820
Yes.

149
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:06,340
Alright, various.

150
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:18,600
Hey, let's make our honeymoon in Australia!

151
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,220
Anywhere you want to go is fine.

152
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:20,880
I'm so happy.

153
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:22,300
Again.

154
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,020
Here I come, yoi-wai-na!

155
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:31,920
Yes.

156
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,200
What are you doing, Otsu?

157
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:37,820
Please, have mercy, Chief.

158
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:41,960
Stubborn people like you won't listen
unless I do something like this.

159
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:43,260
What?

160
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,080
Hey, Kakuda, talk.

161
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,500
F-father...

162
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,560
No, Mr. Ohara.

163
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,600
I don't know, I don't know,
I can't hear you, I can't hear anything.

164
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:55,560
Chief, we're not children,
so enough already.

165
00:08:56,680 --> 00:09:25,200
Ataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataataata!

166
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:33,240
Yay!

167
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:33,720
Yay!

168
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,180
Yay! Dad!

169
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:37,000
Dad!

170
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:38,720
Dad!

171
00:09:39,140 --> 00:09:39,280
Dad!

172
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:39,300
Dad!

173
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:40,680
Dad!

174
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:41,700
Dad!

175
00:09:43,280 --> 00:09:49,960
Dad!

176
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:54,900
Dad!

177
00:09:56,560 --> 00:09:57,680
Eat it! Please, just eat!

178
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:17,700
You've been found out, Chief.

179
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:20,440
Getting off!

180
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:21,820
Wait!

181
00:10:21,980 --> 00:10:22,640
Mr. Ohara!

182
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:30,420
Step on it all the way to Tokyo!

183
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,240
Excuse me, I'm leaving first.

184
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:36,680
He's planning to run off to Tokyo.

185
00:10:39,880 --> 00:10:41,100
Dad!

186
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,940
Please just listen to me.

187
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:48,540
What persistent people!

188
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:51,020
Yaah!

189
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:53,900
Yaah!

190
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,620
Hahaha

191
00:10:55,620 --> 00:10:56,380
There!

192
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:57,880
Ryo-san, it's a net!

193
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,180
Whoa!

194
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:02,340
Whoa, it's flooding!

195
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:02,880
Step forward!

196
00:11:03,260 --> 00:11:04,360
Hahaha

197
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:08,260
Sendō, just keep going
all the way to America!

198
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:09,380
America?

199
00:11:10,280 --> 00:11:11,200
Haah...

200
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:12,880
Kyaa!

201
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,180
You guys!

202
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:21,940
That must have been hard.

203
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:24,520
Chief's stubbornness
really wore me out, too.

204
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,100
Here you go, Ryo-chan. Tea.

205
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:29,240
Thanks.

206
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:31,000
So what about Mr. Kakuda?

207
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,400
He went back to the company.

208
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:35,700
But even he,

209
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,040
sticking with me to the very end,

210
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:38,900
has some real guts.

211
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,320
I'd like to somehow be of use to him.

212
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:43,220
So then,

213
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,200
What are we going to do now, Ryo-chan?

214
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:49,520
Well, at this point we have no
choice but to leave the Chief alone.

215
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,080
We'll do it on our own.

216
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:53,580
Just you watch.

217
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:57,920
We'll hold such a splendid wedding
that the Chief will be blown away.

218
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:14,360
Without Dad?

219
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:20,400
Listen, with the Chief here,
nothing will get settled.

220
00:12:20,860 --> 00:12:23,800
If we wait for him to give a good answer,
who knows how many years it'll take.

221
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,040
But -

222
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:30,960
Yes, maybe that would be best.

223
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:31,900
Mom.

224
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:35,040
I'm sure Dad will forgive us too.

225
00:12:35,700 --> 00:12:39,200
For all his grumbling, he'll miss
you leaving for your husband's home.

226
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,960
Ryo-san, thank you for saying that.

227
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,000
Let's make him resign himself to it.

228
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,280
Please, keep things moving along.

229
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,320
Leave it to us.

230
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:48,760
Let's push ahead quickly.

231
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:49,760
Full speed ahead, then.

232
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:57,600
My.

233
00:12:57,600 --> 00:13:00,380
You didn't go swimming in Tokyo Bay too,
did you?

234
00:13:00,380 --> 00:13:00,940
What?

235
00:13:02,660 --> 00:13:03,560
Hey, dear.

236
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:04,100
What is it?

237
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:06,300
It's about Hiromi...

238
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:09,520
Why don't you forgive her?

239
00:13:09,520 --> 00:13:15,000
You know Mr. Kakuta is a perfectly fine young man,
don't you?

240
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,900
No, I don't want to hear
about that kind of guy.

241
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:22,680
Then at least meet Mr. Kakuta once.

242
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:23,040
What?

243
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:27,060
Meet him properly,
talk with him, and then decide.

244
00:13:28,120 --> 00:13:28,920
Dear...

245
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:37,080
If you don't meet him now, we'll go ahead
and make the wedding arrangements without you.

246
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:39,760
What? By what right?

247
00:13:39,760 --> 00:13:41,020
My right.

248
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:43,320
I am Hiromi's mother.

249
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:46,140
Do you think you raised
that girl all by yourself?

250
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:49,500
No, no, no, I didn't mean it that way.

251
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:52,100
Then you'll meet him, won't you?

252
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:56,720
No, I won't. Some nobody whose
background no one even knows.

253
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,940
I can't just meet him like that.

254
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,700
I will never approve, you hear me?

255
00:14:00,700 --> 00:14:02,400
If you're going to do it, do it on your own.

256
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:05,880
You're a troublesome one, you know.

257
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,300
What "right" do I have

258
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,780
Who do you think you owe this to?

259
00:14:12,900 --> 00:14:14,040
Do whatever you want.

260
00:14:15,780 --> 00:14:16,860
We're fully booked.

261
00:14:17,380 --> 00:14:19,580
I really want to do it a week from now.

262
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,320
What did you say?

263
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,520
That's enough.

264
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:24,420
I'll never ask your
place for anything again.

265
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:27,120
Where next?

266
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,280
Isn't there anything else we can use?

267
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,500
Everything's all set now.

268
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,860
I never expected you to go this far.

269
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,000
Yes, you're right.

270
00:14:40,340 --> 00:14:42,060
If it's come to this,
we're not backing down either.

271
00:14:43,860 --> 00:14:46,720
That's right, that guy was here too.

272
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:50,180
Yes, this is Asakusa Kamen Tsuru speaking.

273
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:52,620
The chairman?

274
00:14:53,140 --> 00:14:54,380
Please hold on a moment.

275
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:57,400
Ryo-chan, long time no see.

276
00:14:58,820 --> 00:15:00,880
Our hotel that's opening soon...

277
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:03,620
Ryo-chan, you can't just suddenly
say something like that to me.

278
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:06,060
It's still a week before the opening.

279
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:08,440
Yeah, the wedding hall's the
only thing that's finished.

280
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:10,980
B-but the interior's
still under construction...

281
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:13,680
February 1st, four years ago...

282
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,940
you were drunk and passed
out in the middle of the road,

283
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:17,860
who was it that walked you home?

284
00:15:18,580 --> 00:15:20,020
When you got caught pissing in the street,

285
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:22,020
who was it that bailed you out?

286
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:25,540
and all that stuff you did
behind the missus's back,

287
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:26,620
should I go ahead and spill it?

288
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:28,560
A-all right, fine.

289
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,520
Hey, I'm not asking for it for free.

290
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:33,140
In return,
I'll make you a Kinshodo Deco-ichi.

291
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:34,700
You got that? Don't screw it up, understand?

292
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:37,220
How about that? We've booked the venue!

293
00:15:39,080 --> 00:15:41,300
It did seem a little pitiful, though.

294
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,100
Just lean on him a little longer.

295
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:49,200
You! What do you think you're
doing during work hours?

296
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:51,120
Too bad.

297
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:53,820
I'm off the clock now, just grilling away.

298
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:55,740
Then you'd better hurry up and head home.

299
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:59,680
Chief, before you go home,
I have something to say.

300
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:03,160
We've just settled on the wedding venue and date,
so please take note.

301
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:07,340
I bet Hiromi will look
beautiful in her wedding dress.

302
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:09,260
If you go meddling!

303
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:42,580
Dad, just put this on for a sec.

304
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:44,660
Oh my,

305
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:04,260
Daddy!

306
00:17:27,020 --> 00:17:28,420
It's all right, Hiromi.

307
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:31,060
Your father will definitely come.

308
00:17:32,060 --> 00:17:32,520
But...

309
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:34,760
Don't worry.

310
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:37,680
He just can't help loving you, you know.

311
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,560
Dear,

312
00:17:47,460 --> 00:17:48,180
You're burning up.

313
00:17:48,180 --> 00:17:50,580
Hiromi, call the doctor.

314
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:51,660
Hiromi?

315
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:52,760
Yes,

316
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:59,480
Anyway,
just keep him warm and let him rest today.

317
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,680
Thank you very much.

318
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:15,020
Hiromi, you should go to bed now.

319
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:16,920
Tomorrow is an important day.

320
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:18,480
It's fine, let me do it.

321
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:20,620
You should rest first, Mom.

322
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,980
Because it's my fault.

323
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,200
Because I caused you worry,

324
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:27,880
Dad hasn't been sleeping properly at night.

325
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:28,840
But you...

326
00:18:29,720 --> 00:18:32,140
Please, I only have today.

327
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:34,360
Until the wedding tomorrow,

328
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:35,680
I'm still an Ohara daughter,

329
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,040
and I want to be Dad's child.

330
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:39,800
Hiromi.

331
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:44,800
Hiromi.

332
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:45,180
Hiromi.

333
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:49,160
No! I won't allow this marriage yet!

334
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:50,120
Hiromi!

335
00:18:52,940 --> 00:18:53,820
No!

336
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,400
Thank goodness, the fever's gone down.

337
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:18,760
Dad.

338
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:22,700
Dad, thank you for
everything all these years.

339
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:26,460
Hiromi is getting married to Hideo today.

340
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:30,220
I wanted you to be
happier for me than anyone.

341
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,500
But it was my fault.

342
00:19:34,020 --> 00:19:37,620
I should have thought more about you.

343
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:42,340
Hiromi.

344
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:43,660
Hiromi-san, it's about time.

345
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,500
Come on, don't worry about your father.

346
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:50,660
Once the ceremony's over,
Mom will come straight back.

347
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:52,900
The ceremony starts at twelve,
hurry up, hurry up!

348
00:19:53,580 --> 00:19:53,900
Yes.

349
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:09,780
The Chief isn't coming, is he.

350
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:12,140
He collapsed with a cold.
There's no way he could come.

351
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:25,020
Hiromi.

352
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:29,120
I should have thought
more about your father.

353
00:20:32,040 --> 00:20:33,020
I...

354
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:36,600
Damn, I caught a cold. I'm going to bed.

355
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:37,520
Dad.

356
00:20:37,520 --> 00:20:40,340
No, I still have work to do.

357
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:45,740
I was so stubborn,
without even considering Hiromi's feelings.

358
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:46,680
Daddy.

359
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:50,980
Did you come to pick me up, Hiromi?

360
00:20:50,980 --> 00:20:51,440
Mm-hm.

361
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:54,240
What will you be when you grow up, Hiromi?

362
00:20:54,780 --> 00:20:56,260
Daddy's bride.

363
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:59,420
Daddy's bride, is it?

364
00:21:01,100 --> 00:21:02,840
She said she wants to
enter the police academy.

365
00:21:02,840 --> 00:21:04,260
No, no, absolutely not.

366
00:21:04,260 --> 00:21:07,200
I can't let you take on such a tough job.

367
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:09,440
Go to university properly.

368
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:13,300
She said she has a boyfriend.

369
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,940
You look beautiful, Hiromi.

370
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:27,780
It's almost time, though.

371
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:28,940
Just...

372
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:31,560
Could you wait just five more minutes?

373
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:37,520
Papa.

374
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:39,460
Hiromi.

375
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:46,480
Hiromi... Hiromi.

376
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:48,160
Hiromi.

377
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:58,240
Hiromi.

378
00:21:58,240 --> 00:22:02,360
Let's do our best so
your father will be happy.

379
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:04,400
Yes.

380
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:07,740
Sensō-ji! Hurry!

381
00:22:07,740 --> 00:22:11,300
Kakuta and I have been
friends since elementary school.

382
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:14,120
When we were students, Kakuta was usually...

383
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:27,740
They look so happy.

384
00:22:27,740 --> 00:22:32,700
Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss! Kiss!

385
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:34,380
Stop right there!

386
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:38,860
Dad!

387
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:40,500
Oh no, Nakagawa, stop him!

388
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:43,240
Chief, are you feeling all right?

389
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:44,540
Chief!

390
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:45,440
Shut up!

391
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:49,660
Everyone, I'm the bride's father.

392
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:52,260
I am against this marriage.

393
00:22:55,260 --> 00:22:56,280
I was opposed.

394
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,980
without even considering
how sad Hiromi would be.

395
00:22:58,980 --> 00:23:01,400
I kept avoiding Kakuta-kun.

396
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:04,620
If my subordinates hadn't forced
the ceremony to take place,

397
00:23:04,620 --> 00:23:05,844
I... I...

398
00:23:05,894 --> 00:23:09,240
I would have had to live with that
regret for the rest of my life.

399
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:11,060
Everyone, thank you for today.

400
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,920
And Kakuta-kun, I'm sorry.

401
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:17,760
Dad.

402
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:19,585
Hideo-kun, Hiromi,

403
00:23:19,635 --> 00:23:21,980
please take good care of my daughter.

404
00:23:21,980 --> 00:23:24,120
Y-yes, leave it to us.

405
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:28,740
Alright, I'm taking the picture now. Smile!

406
00:23:29,420 --> 00:23:30,980
Okay, pose!

407
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,140
What a lovely ceremony that was.

408
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:42,220
Alright, Ryotsu,
let's hit one more place, one more!

409
00:23:42,220 --> 00:23:45,520
Chief, let's head home soon.
You've caught a cold, right?

410
00:23:46,240 --> 00:23:49,040
What did you say?
I'll make you write an apology letter!

411
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:51,340
Fine, fine, let's go.

412
00:23:51,340 --> 00:23:53,180
Ten places, twenty places, whatever.

413
00:23:53,180 --> 00:23:54,660
Yes, that's the spirit!

414
00:23:54,660 --> 00:23:57,240
Tan-tan-katan.

415
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:59,240
Tan-tan-katan.

416
00:23:59,240 --> 00:24:01,080
Ha ha ha ha

417
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:07,960
Nakagawa, go after the Chief right now!

418
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:10,560
We're getting back my
paper bag he took by mistake.

419
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:13,960
Why do I have to help get it back?

420
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:17,460
Because it also has your nude photos in it,
that's why!

421
00:24:17,840 --> 00:24:21,280
Get the top-secret photos back this time,
got it? Thanks.

422
00:24:29,840 --> 00:24:32,700
Even if we stop the clocks,

423
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps passing by.

424
00:24:39,300 --> 00:24:42,640
Crying with a scrunched-up face,

425
00:24:44,360 --> 00:24:48,120
let's laugh it off and keep on living.

426
00:24:50,340 --> 00:24:53,020
Even if today

427
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:57,920
is rainy,

428
00:24:59,560 --> 00:25:03,440
tomorrow will be sunny.

429
00:25:04,620 --> 00:25:13,860
Bye-bye, let's wave,
unpleasant things, goodbye.

430
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:23,980
Oh yeah, let's live as we like,
good things will come.

431
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:30,200
Outside the door,
the stars are calling to you.

432
00:25:36,480 --> 00:25:42,440
Thank you for watching.

